2945.description:
The full Committee on Energy and Commerce held a markup on Tuesday, April 5, 2011, at 10:00 a.m. in 2123 Rayburn House Office Building.  The markup included the following legislation:

H.R. 1343, a bill to Clarify NTIA and RUS Authority to return unused or reclaimed funds made available for broadband awards in the American Recovery and Reinvestment Act of 2009 to the Treasury of the United States, pending a markup of that legislation in the Subcommittee on Communications and Technology to be held on Friday, April 1, 2011; 
H.R. 1217, a bill to repeal the Prevention and Public Health Fund, as reported by the Subcommittee on Health; 
H.R. 1216, a bill to amend the Public Health Service Act to convert funding for graduate medical education in qualified teaching health centers from direct appropriations to an authorization of appropriations, as reported by the Subcommittee on Health; 
H.R. 1215, a bill to amend title V of the Social Security Act to convert funding for personal responsibility education programs from direct appropriations to an authorization of appropriations, as reported by the Subcommittee on Health; 
H.R. 1214, a bill to repeal mandatory funding for school-based health center construction, as reported by the Subcommittee on Health; and, 
H.R. 1213, a bill to repeal mandatory funding provided to States in the Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act to establish American Health Benefit Exchanges, as reported by the Subcommittee on Health. 
All of the health-related bills were reported by the Subcommittee on Health without amendment from their introduced versions.

